      en: "Lombok is world-renowned as a premier producer of high-quality South Sea Pearls, particularly the rare 'Golden Pearl' and 'Silver Pearl.' The island's pristine, nutrient-rich coastal waters and sheltered bays provide the ideal environment for the Pinctada maxima oyster, the world's largest pearl-producing oyster. Pearl farming is a delicate and long-term agricultural process, requiring up to two to three years for a single pearl to develop. The industry is a major economic driver for the island, with many farms located around the Sekotong peninsula and the Gili Islands. Lombok pearls are prized by international jewelers for their exceptional luster, size, and thick nacre, making them some of the most sought-after organic gemstones in the world. Geography K11 — Marine Aquaculture and Luxury Commodities."
